#
#	OpenTPW example mod: a lamp post whose light the object's script switches and colours (docs/LIGHTS.md)
#	Every number marked "OpenTPW's own value" is a choice of this example, not a value of the original game.
#
Info.Id			65000		placeholder: objects.json replaces it with the object's own id
Info.Name		"Lamp Post"
Info.IsChoosable	0		guests never choose a lamp
Info.HasQueue		0
Info.WhichUIType	3		a feature (the build menu's Features tab)

# The footprint: one cell, no entrance and no exit.
Info.Shape
---
*
---

Upgrades[0].CostOfUpgrade		40		OpenTPW's own value
Upgrades[0].CostOfResearch		0		An object without research cost starts researched
Research.Group		0
Info.PreviewAnimNum		0

# [EXT:object-lights] The model carries one light dummy, number 0 (a warm white of radius 60 model units); these keys tune it without
# touching the model. Colours are percent of full, the radius is in model units (0.2 engine units each: 70 is 14 units, seven cells).
Lights[0].Radius	70		overrides the 60 the model carries
Lights[0].On		1		the light starts on (the default); 0 would start it off until the script enables it
